---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs title="Installation">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Installation</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Sprõut requires React 19 and Tailwind CSS 4. Sidebar comes from npm; your
    app builds their styles.
  </p>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Local preview</h2>
    <p>
      The first release is not published yet. To try this checkout, install
      dependencies at the repository root and run <code>pnpm dev</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Package setup</h2>
    <p>
      After the first npm release, add the package to your React application.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="pnpm add @tulipfarm/sprout" />
    <p>
      Import Sprõut after Tailwind in your existing stylesheet. Source
      registration is included: no JavaScript theme config or extra reset is
      needed.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      title="app.css"
      code={`@import "tailwindcss";
@import "@tulipfarm/sprout/styles.css";`}
    />
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="App.tsx"
      code={`import {
  Sidebar,
  SidebarProvider,
  SidebarTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/sidebar";

<SidebarProvider className="min-h-dvh">
  <Sidebar label="Main navigation">
    {/* Compose your navigation here. */}
  </Sidebar>
  <main><SidebarTrigger /></main>
</SidebarProvider>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Install through shadcn</h2>
    <p>
      The bootstrap registry item installs the npm dependency and adds the CSS
      import. It does not copy or overwrite your component files. The hosted
      command becomes available after publication and deployment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Inspect the <a href="/r/sprout.json" class="underline underline-offset-4"
        >registry item</a
      >. The install contract is exercised with shadcn 4.22.0 and Tailwind 4.3.3
      against a packed local package.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Existing shadcn applications</h2>
    <p>
      Keep your existing imports and theme. Sprõut uses its own <code
        >--sprout-*</code
      > variables and semantic utilities. No shared <code>--primary</code> or <code
        >--background</code
      > variables are replaced.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tailwind utility prefixes are not supported in this preview. Sprõut and
      shadcn do not promise identical props. Use aliases if both libraries
      export a component with the same name.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
